er what you  read just a couple days ago than what  you'd read  like six months ago this is also what  cal newport suggests  in his book deep work i also made a  video on that if you want to check it  out i'll leave the link here  and i think that's why so many great  ideas and projects come  out of the thesis project because you  get to dedicate  a full year or two to just reading  tons of books and other research i also  have some tips and tricks on how to  remember everything you read  so make sure you check that out if  that's something you're interested in  in organizations i think it will be so  valuable if they encouraged employees to  take time  off work for learning new skills or  information  apparently google gives engineers one  day a week  to work on anything they want and  apparently almost half of their profit  generators  are from these independent projects  at the societal level the internet is  really the best tool for connections but  according to steven johnson  the way that we use it by filtering out  like  99.9 of the irrelevant information  it can sometimes take away the  serendipitous aspect of  the internet anyways that's it i hope  you guys found that interesting  this is one of those books that i will  just pick up and read  over and over again from time to time  because it's just like really inspiring  and it's full of fun anecdotes and  i feel like i take away something new  every time i read it so if you're  interested in reading the full book i'll  leave the link in my description  if you're interested in book reviews and  the creative process  i have another video where i talk about  the book deep work  by cal newport where he breaks down some  of the skills  that's going to make you really valuable  in the  digital world so check that out  and and i'll see you guys in the next  video  [Music]  bye  you
 

